# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/chain_thornwick.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event tamsin_second_letter
# en: Insufferable AND Rude
title [1faa8e] = 让人受不了，而且没礼貌
# en: A second letter from Thornwick, in the same quick hand. "Insufferable AND rude. Noted. I'm giving you one more chance, because I'm a generous person and because my roommate bet me you'd never answer. Prove her wrong. T. Reed."
text [77fe54] = 荆木学院的第二封信，同样潦草的笔迹。“让人受不了，而且没礼貌。记下了。我再给你一次机会，因为我是个大方的人，也因为我室友跟我打赌说你永远不会回信。证明她错了。T. 里德。”
# en: A second letter with a green Thornwick seal on a dormitory pillow, the word "NOTED" underlined three times.
scene [85442f] = 宿舍枕头上放着第二封信，盖着荆木学院的绿色封蜡，“记下了”三个字下面划了三道线。
# en: Write back, finally
opt.left.label [ebbeda] = 终于回信
# en: You write back, grudgingly at first and then not at all grudgingly. Four pages. The answer comes within a week, with a postscript: "My roommate owes me a pie. Thank you."
opt.left.say.1 [b76498] = 你回了信，一开始很不情愿，后来一点也不。四页。不到一星期回信就到了，附言写着：“我室友欠我一个派。谢谢你。”
# en: Let it lie
opt.right.label [9e1bb5] = 随它去
# en: You leave it on the pillow. Somewhere across the hills, a roommate wins a pie. You'll never know what you missed, which is how it should be, probably.
opt.right.say.1 [2d2a7b] = 你把信留在枕头上。山那边的某处，一个室友赢了一个派。你永远不会知道自己错过了什么，大概本该如此。

@event tamsin_letter_gossip
# en: News From Thornwick
title [ab4189] = 荆木来信
# en: {Tamsin has written again, six pages of Thornwick gossip with sketches of the professors in the margins.|Another letter from Tamsin, signed "your rival, nemesis and only friend west of the hills".|Tamsin's letter is mostly a drawing of their illusion professor as a goat.} {~Their head of house has banned whistling.|Someone at Thornwick set the library on fire, a little.|They want to know if Lumenhold's food is really as bad as everyone says.} Answering properly would take an evening.
text [2b961c] = {塔姆辛又来信了，六页荆木学院的八卦，页边画满了教授们的速写。|塔姆辛又来信了，署名“你的对手、宿敌，以及山这边唯一的朋友”。|塔姆辛的信大半是一幅画，画的是 TA 的幻术教授变成了一只山羊。} {~TA 的学院院长禁止了吹口哨。|荆木学院有人把图书馆点着了，一点点。|TA 想知道流明堡的伙食是不是真像大家说的那么糟。} 认真回信得花一个晚上。
# en: A letter with a green seal open on a desk, its margins full of tiny unflattering sketches of Thornwick professors.
scene [23ad0a] = 桌上摊开一封盖着绿色封蜡的信，页边画满了荆木学院教授们小小的、毫不留情的速写。
# en: Write back at length
opt.left.label [7bb28c] = 写一封长信回去
# en: {~You write till the candle gutters, with sketches of your own professors, and pay the extra postage. Tamsin's reply calls your drawing of Thorne "libellous and correct".|Five pages back, with the castle's gossip and your worst week. They answer the worst week first.}
opt.left.say.1 [d77190] = {~你写到蜡烛燃尽，附上你自己画的教授速写，还付了超重的邮费。塔姆辛的回信说你画的索恩教授“诽谤，但准确”。|回了五页，有城堡的八卦，也有你最糟的一周。TA 先回了那最糟的一周。}
# en: A few lines and a sketch
opt.right.label [79d945] = 几行字和一幅速写
# en: {~A short note and a drawing of a gargoyle. Tamsin writes back that it's "the most Lumenhold thing ever sent through the post".|Three lines. Tamsin replies with three pages, offended and delighted.}
opt.right.say.1 [bd7f6a] = {~一张短笺和一幅石像鬼的画。塔姆辛回信说，这是“邮路上寄过的最流明堡的东西”。|三行字。塔姆辛回了三页，又气又乐。}

@event tamsin_letter_questions
# en: Twenty Questions
title [87b695] = 二十个问题
# en: {Tamsin's letter is a numbered list of twenty questions about life at Lumenhold, from "Is the lake haunted?" to "What do you eat for breakfast?"|Another list of questions. Number seven is "Who is the most annoying person at your school?"|Questions again. "Be honest," says number one. "Number twenty can be a lie."} {~Number twelve asks about your exams.|Number fifteen asks about the lake.|Number nineteen just says "Are you happy?"}
text [562a2f] = {塔姆辛的信是一份编了号的清单，二十个关于流明堡生活的问题，从“湖里闹鬼吗？”到“你早餐吃什么？”。|又是一张问题清单。第七个是“你们学校最烦人的是谁？”|又是问题。“说实话，”第一个写道。“第二十个可以撒谎。”} {~第十二个问你的考试。|第十五个问那座湖。|第十九个只写着“你快乐吗？”}
# en: A letter numbered down the margin from one to twenty, each line a question, a student chewing a quill over the answers.
scene [06c1b8] = 一封信的页边从一编号到二十，每一行都是一个问题，一个学生咬着羽毛笔思考答案。
# en: Answer every one honestly
opt.left.label [68babc] = 每一个都老实回答
# en: {~Twenty honest answers, even number nineteen. It's harder than it looks. Their reply begins, "Thank you for nineteen."|You answer the lot. Writing it down, you learn a few things about yourself.}
opt.left.say.1 [22cc07] = {~二十个老实的回答，连第十九个也是。这比看起来难。TA 的回信开头是：“谢谢你回答了第十九个。”|你全答了。写下来的时候，你对自己多了几分了解。}
# en: Make the answers outrageous
opt.right.label [2a7503] = 把答案编得离谱些
# en: {~The lake is haunted by a choir of geese. Breakfast is boiled bricks. Tamsin's reply is two pages of laughter and a request for "the true answers, eventually".|You invent a Lumenhold of dragons and duels before dawn. Tamsin believes none of it and asks for more.}
opt.right.say.1 [de8161] = {~湖里闹的是一支鹅组成的合唱团。早餐是水煮砖头。塔姆辛回了两页笑声，并要求“以后告诉我真正的答案”。|你编出了一个有龙、黎明前决斗的流明堡。塔姆辛一个字也不信，还要你再多写点。}

@event tamsin_letter_trouble
# en: A Short Letter
title [fc5c66] = 一封短信
# en: Tamsin's letter is one page, which has never happened. They failed their illusion examination, the one thing they were good at, and their grandmother's theatre has been sold. There's a sentence crossed out so hard the nib went through the paper.
text [b7b79a] = 塔姆辛的信只有一页，这从来没有过。TA 的幻术考试挂了，那是 TA 唯一擅长的东西，祖母的剧团也卖掉了。有一句话被划得太狠，笔尖戳穿了纸。
# en: A single short page with a green seal, the handwriting cramped and unsteady, a blot where a sentence was crossed out hard.
scene [c5d9d6] = 一页短短的信盖着绿色封蜡，字迹局促而颤抖，一处墨渍是被狠狠划掉的一句话。
# en: Write back that night
opt.left.label [bb6a52] = 当晚就回信
# en: You write until two in the morning: the time you failed, what helped, a list of everything they're good at that isn't illusion. Their next letter is six pages again, and the first line is "You idiot, you made me cry in the refectory."
opt.left.say.1 [8541b5] = 你一直写到凌晨两点：你挂科的那次，什么帮了你，还有一张清单，列出 TA 除了幻术之外擅长的所有事。TA 的下一封信又是六页，第一行是：“你这个笨蛋，害我在膳堂里哭了。”
# en: Send them something instead
opt.right.label [75de79] = 改寄点东西过去
# en: You send a parcel: Mabel's best biscuits, a book of plays, a drawing of a gargoyle holding a sign that says "RETAKE". Tamsin writes back that the gargoyle is on their wall now, and that they passed.
opt.right.say.1 [866768] = 你寄了个包裹：梅布尔茶馆最好的饼干、一本剧本集、一幅石像鬼举着“补考”牌子的画。塔姆辛回信说那只石像鬼现在挂在 TA 墙上，而且 TA 补考过了。

@event tamsin_letter_asks_secret
# en: A Small Favour
title [24d010] = 一个小忙
# en: Tamsin's letter is cheerful until the last paragraph. "Small favour. Thornwick's duelling captain wants to know Lumenhold's tournament order. Just the order. Everyone does it, honestly. I'd owe you." The underline is very neat, as if they did it twice.
text [fdb7c9] = 塔姆辛的信一直很开心，直到最后一段。“帮个小忙。荆木的决斗队长想知道流明堡的比赛出场顺序。只要顺序。大家都这么干，真的。我会欠你一个人情。”那道下划线非常整齐，像是划了两遍。
# en: A letter half-read on a desk, a single paragraph underlined twice, a student staring out of a window at the hills.
scene [114522] = 一封读了一半的信放在桌上，有一段话下面划了两道线，一个学生望着窗外的群山发呆。
# en: Send the real order
opt.left.label [21dd30] = 寄出真实的顺序
# en: You write it out: who fights first, who last. It feels like nothing at all until you post it, and then it feels like a stone. Tamsin's reply thanks you, too warmly.
opt.left.say.1 [817ae0] = 你写了出来：谁先上，谁最后。在寄出之前，这感觉什么也不是；寄出之后，它像一块石头。塔姆辛回信道谢，热情得过了头。
# en: Send a false one
opt.right.label [bdb397] = 寄一份假的
# en: You invent an order, plausible and wrong. At the tournament, Thornwick's captain looks baffled for the whole first round. Tamsin's next letter is short and doesn't mention it, which is how you know they know.
opt.right.say.1 [9998b8] = 你编了一个顺序，合理，但全错。比赛上，荆木的队长整个第一轮都一脸茫然。塔姆辛的下一封信很短，只字未提，你就是这样知道 TA 知道了。
# en: Say no, and say why
opt.refuse.label [f281a1] = 拒绝，并说明理由
# en: "Ask me anything else," you write. Their reply is a week late and very polite. Then, a fortnight after: "You were right. Sorry. Still friends?" You write back yes before you've finished reading.
opt.refuse.say.1 [15d176] = “问我别的什么都行，”你写道。TA 的回信晚了一个星期，非常客气。又过了两个星期：“你是对的。对不起。还是朋友吗？”你还没读完就回了“是”。

@event tamsin_letter_offers_secret
# en: Their Turn
title [9873fa] = 轮到 TA 了
# en: Folded inside Tamsin's letter is a second paper: Thornwick's whole plan for this year's contest, every pairing, every trick. "Fair's fair," they've written. "Burn it or use it. I won't ask which."
text [570c1c] = 塔姆辛的信里夹着另一张纸：荆木学院今年比赛的全盘计划，每一组对阵，每一个花招。“公平起见，”TA 写道，“烧了它，或者用它。我不会问你选了哪个。”
# en: A folded paper inside a letter, covered in diagrams of duelling circles and arrows, a student holding it at arm's length as if it were hot.
scene [cbfb50] = 一封信里夹着一张折起的纸，画满了决斗圈和箭头的图示，一个学生伸直胳膊拿着它，仿佛它烫手。
# en: Use it
opt.left.label [77da81] = 用它
# en: You keep the plan and study it until you know it better than Thornwick does. It will help. You can't quite look at your own reflection while you read it.
opt.left.say.1 [300161] = 你留下那份计划，研究到比荆木的人还熟。它会有用的。读它的时候，你有点不敢看镜子里的自己。
# en: Burn it unread
opt.right.label [f39f04] = 看都不看就烧掉
# en: You burn it in the candle without unfolding it, and write back that you did. Their reply has one line: "I knew you would. That's why I sent it." You're still not sure if it was a test.
opt.right.say.1 [672e02] = 你没展开就在烛火上烧了它，并回信告诉 TA。TA 的回信只有一行：“我就知道你会。所以我才寄给你。”你到现在也不确定那是不是一场考验。

@event tamsin_confession
# en: What I Was Sent to Do
title [f7c453] = 我被派来做的事
# en: Tamsin's letter is long and the hand is unsteady. "I have to tell you. The first letter wasn't random. Thornwick set some of us to write to Lumenhold students and report back. I reported for two letters. Then I liked you, and I stopped, and I've been ashamed ever since. You can stop writing. I'd understand."
text [d82e6f] = 塔姆辛的信很长，字迹颤抖。“我必须告诉你。第一封信不是随机的。荆木让我们中的一些人写信给流明堡的学生，然后回去汇报。我汇报了两封信的内容。后来我喜欢上了你，就停了，从那以后一直觉得羞愧。你可以不再写信了。我能理解。”
# en: A long letter in a shaky hand spread across a desk, a green seal broken beside it, a student reading with one hand over their mouth.
scene [71b1c0] = 一封长信摊在桌上，字迹颤抖，旁边是一枚碎开的绿色封蜡，一个学生一手捂着嘴读着。
# en: Forgive them
opt.left.label [6c4629] = 原谅 TA
# en: You write back one line: "Third letter onwards, then. That's when I started liking you too." Their reply is the longest yet, and the first not signed with an insult.
opt.left.say.1 [b80866] = 你只回了一行：“那就从第三封信算起吧。我也是从那时开始喜欢你的。”TA 的回信是有史以来最长的一封，也是第一封署名里没有一句损人话的。
# en: Ask what they reported
opt.right.label [0e7b6d] = 问 TA 汇报了什么
# en: They tell you, exactly: the food, the weather, your opinion of Professor Thorne. Nothing that mattered. "I made it boring on purpose," they write. You laugh, and then you forgive them anyway.
opt.right.say.1 [232dfa] = TA 一五一十地告诉了你：伙食、天气、你对索恩教授的看法。没有一件要紧的事。“我故意写得很无聊，”TA 写道。你笑了，然后还是原谅了 TA。

@event tamsin_letter_after
# en: After Graduation
title [f78127] = 毕业之后
# en: Tamsin's letter has a map on the back with two towns circled: Lumenhold and Thornwick, and a line between them. "After graduation, there'll be no school to be rivals for. What are we, then?" Under it, smaller: "Don't answer that. Answer it."
text [275f1a] = 塔姆辛的信背面画着一张地图，圈出了两座城：流明堡和荆木，中间连着一条线。“毕业以后，就没有学校让我们较劲了。那我们算什么？”下面一行小字：“别回答。回答我。”
# en: A letter with a green seal and a pressed flower, a map of the realm sketched on the back with two towns circled.
scene [4c98cd] = 一封盖着绿色封蜡、夹着压花的信，背面草草画着王国的地图，圈出了两座城。
# en: "Friends. Obviously."
opt.left.label [28c81e] = “朋友。显然。”
# en: You write it in letters an inch high. Their reply has the map again, with a third town circled halfway between: "Meeting point. Every spring. Bring biscuits."
opt.left.say.1 [2b1665] = 你用一寸高的字写了下来。TA 的回信又附上了那张地图，在两城正中间圈了第三座小镇：“碰头地点。每年春天。带饼干。”
# en: "Still rivals. Obviously."
opt.right.label [292e36] = “还是对手。显然。”
# en: "Excellent," they write back. "I was worried you'd go soft." Under it, very small: "Friends too, though. Obviously."
opt.right.say.1 [8691d3] = “太好了，”TA 回信说，“我还担心你会变软呢。”下面是很小的字：“不过也是朋友。显然。”

@event rival_return_visit
# en: To Thornwick
title [7f07af] = 前往荆木
# en: This year it's Lumenhold's turn to visit. A barge leaves for Thornwick at dawn with a delegation of students who have been told to behave. {met(tamsin): Tamsin has written three letters about it. The last one just says "COME".|Thornwick has, by all accounts, better plumbing.}
text [88f77d] = 今年轮到流明堡回访了。一艘驳船将在黎明时分载着一支被叮嘱要守规矩的学生代表团驶向荆木学院。{met(tamsin): 塔姆辛为这事写了三封信。最后一封只写着“来”。|据大家说，荆木学院的水管比这儿好。}
# en: A barge full of Lumenhold students arriving at a rival academy of green-roofed towers, a crowd of green-robed students waiting on the jetty.
scene [88b117] = 一艘满载流明堡学生的驳船抵达一座绿顶塔楼林立的对手学院，码头上等着一群穿绿袍的学生。
# en: Join the delegation
opt.go.label [81e864] = 加入代表团
# en: Two days across the hills. The barge fare is yours.
opt.go.hint [6f7ab8] = 翻山越岭两天。船费你自己出。
# en: Tamsin is on the jetty, smaller than their letters and louder, holding a sign with your name spelled wrong on purpose. They show you every corner of Thornwick and argue that each one beats Lumenhold. They're mostly wrong.
opt.go.say.1 [e034ec] = 塔姆辛就在码头上，比信里矮，也比信里吵，举着一块故意把你名字拼错的牌子。TA 带你看遍了荆木的每个角落，坚称每一处都比流明堡强。大多数时候 TA 是错的。
# en: Thornwick's towers are green-roofed and smug, and their plumbing really is better. A student in green follows you around the library, asking about the lake.
opt.go.say.2 [d86a94] = 荆木学院的塔楼顶着绿瓦，一副得意洋洋的样子，他们的水管确实更好。一个穿绿袍的学生在图书馆里一直跟着你，打听那座湖的事。
# en: Stay at the castle
opt.stay.label [04365a] = 留在城堡
# en: A quiet weekend with half the school gone.
opt.stay.hint [2234e2] = 半个学校都走了，一个安静的周末。
# en: You stay. The castle is wonderfully quiet. Tamsin's next letter is very short, and sulks, and then forgives you on the last line.
opt.stay.say.1 [4ce199] = 你留下了。城堡安静得美妙。塔姆辛的下一封信非常短，在赌气，然后在最后一行原谅了你。
# en: The castle is half empty and wholly peaceful. You read in the window seat all weekend and don't miss Thornwick at all.
opt.stay.say.2 [638ff5] = 城堡空了一半，也彻底安宁了。你整个周末都窝在窗边座位上看书，一点也不想念荆木。

@event rival_contest
# en: The Inter-School Contest
title [451f5d] = 校际比赛
# en: The inter-school contest, at Lumenhold this year, before both schools and half the village. You've made the team. {met(tamsin): In the final, the name opposite yours is Tamsin Reed. They wave from across the ring, apologetically, and then stop smiling.|In the final, a Thornwick illusionist faces you, smiling far too much.}{flag(thornwick_secrets): You know every trick they've planned.|}
text [01c439] = 校际比赛今年在流明堡举行，两校师生和半个村子都来了。你入选了队伍。{met(tamsin): 决赛里，你对面的名字是塔姆辛·里德。TA 隔着赛场冲你挥手，带着歉意，然后收起了笑容。|决赛里，一个荆木的幻术师站在你对面，笑得过分灿烂。}{flag(thornwick_secrets): 他们计划的每一个花招你都知道。|}
# en: A packed duelling arena under banners of blue and green, two duellists facing each other in the chalk ring, a crowd on its feet.
scene [1dd393] = 座无虚席的决斗场，蓝绿两色旗帜高悬，两名决斗者在粉笔圈里对峙，观众全都站了起来。
# en: Fight to win
opt.left.label [0f68e4] = 全力求胜
# en: You counter every planned trick before it's cast. Lumenhold wins the contest, and the castle roars. {met(tamsin): Tamsin shakes your hand afterwards and holds on too long. "You read the plan," they say quietly. "Good." You can't tell if they mean it.|}
opt.left.say.1 [053f35] = 每一个预先计划的花招，你都在对方出手前化解了。流明堡赢下了比赛，整座城堡都在欢呼。{met(tamsin): 赛后塔姆辛和你握手，握得太久了。“你看了那份计划，”TA 轻声说。“很好。”你分辨不出 TA 是不是真心的。|}
# en: Knowing the plan isn't enough: they change it in the ring. Thornwick takes the cup. The plan, in your pocket, feels heavier than ever.
opt.left.say.2 [7a8a18] = 光知道计划是不够的：他们在场上改了。荆木捧走了奖杯。口袋里的那份计划，从没这么沉过。
# en: An honest win, hard and close. Lumenhold takes the cup and carries you round the arena. {met(tamsin): Tamsin is on the ground laughing. "Next year," they gasp. "Next year I'll flatten you."|}
opt.left.say.3 [d0c2e2] = 一场光明正大的胜利，艰难而胶着。流明堡捧起奖杯，抬着你绕场一周。{met(tamsin): 塔姆辛躺在地上笑。“明年，”TA 喘着气说，“明年我要把你打趴下。”|}
# en: You lose by a breath. Thornwick sings all the way back to their barge. {met(tamsin): Tamsin helps you up and doesn't gloat, not once, which you'll never forget.|}
opt.left.say.4 [668fb9] = 你以毫厘之差输了。荆木的人一路唱着歌回到驳船上。{met(tamsin): 塔姆辛把你拉起来，一次也没有炫耀，这一点你永远不会忘记。|}
# en: Fight clean and generous
opt.right.label [928af5] = 打得干净又大度
# en: You fight well and fairly, and when you have them down you let them stand before the next exchange. You lose on points. The crowd stands for both of you anyway, and Lyra, in the stands, actually claps.
opt.right.say.1 [fbea80] = 你打得漂亮而公平，把对手击倒后，还让 TA 站起来再进行下一回合。你按积分输了。观众依然为你们两个起立鼓掌，看台上的莱拉居然也拍了手。

@event rival_last_match
# en: The Last Match
title [bf66e5] = 最后一场比赛
# en: The last match of your year against Thornwick's: an exhibition on the lawn, lanterns in the trees, nothing at stake but four years of grudges. {met(tamsin): Tamsin has asked to be your opponent. "For the record," they say. "Ours."|Thornwick's final-years have brought cake, which feels like a trick.}
text [8a2019] = 你们这一届和荆木同届的最后一场比赛：草坪上的表演赛，树上挂着灯笼，赌注只有四年的积怨。{met(tamsin): 塔姆辛申请当你的对手。“为了记录，”TA 说。“我们俩的。”|荆木的毕业生带来了蛋糕，感觉像个圈套。}
# en: An evening exhibition match on the lawn between two academies, lanterns strung between the trees, final-year students in blue and green laughing in the ring.
scene [d7aa4a] = 两所学院在草坪上的傍晚表演赛，灯笼挂在树间，穿蓝袍和绿袍的毕业生在场中大笑。
# en: Give it everything
opt.left.label [607b0e] = 全力以赴
# en: You win the last exchange of your schooling against Thornwick, and the lawn erupts. {met(tamsin): Tamsin, flat on the grass, laughs up at the lanterns. "Fine," they say. "Fine. Record's yours."|}
opt.left.say.1 [163d65] = 你赢下了学生时代对荆木的最后一次交锋，草坪上一片沸腾。{met(tamsin): 塔姆辛平躺在草地上，冲着灯笼大笑。“好吧，”TA 说。“好吧。纪录归你了。”|}
# en: You lose, gloriously, and lie on the grass looking at the lanterns. {met(tamsin): Tamsin lies down next to you. "Record's mine," they say, and then, quieter, "I'll miss this."|}
opt.left.say.2 [9110fe] = 你输了，输得很漂亮，躺在草地上看着灯笼。{met(tamsin): 塔姆辛在你旁边躺下。“纪录归我了，”TA 说，然后更轻地说：“我会想念这个的。”|}
# en: Turn it into a show
opt.right.label [f31225] = 把它变成一场表演
# en: You turn the match into a performance, illusions and flourishes and a duel that never lands a blow. {met(tamsin): Tamsin catches on at once and plays along. The two schools applaud the same thing for the first time in a century.|Both schools applaud the same thing for the first time in a century.}
opt.right.say.1 [cf1fab] = 你把比赛变成了一场演出，幻术、花哨的动作，一场从没真正命中过的决斗。{met(tamsin): 塔姆辛立刻会意，配合着演了下去。一百年来，两所学校第一次为同一件事鼓掌。|一百年来，两所学校第一次为同一件事鼓掌。}

@event tamsin_farewell
# en: Across the Hills
title [d009b3] = 山那边
# en: At the barge landing, before Thornwick's delegation leaves for the last time, Tamsin gives you a small parcel. Inside: every letter you ever sent them, tied with string. "So you can read how insufferable you were," they say. "I kept copies. Obviously."
text [bedb5b] = 在驳船码头，荆木的代表团最后一次离开之前，塔姆辛递给你一个小包裹。里面是你寄给 TA 的每一封信，用绳子捆着。“好让你读读自己当年有多让人受不了，”TA 说。“我留了副本。显然。”
# en: Two students at a barge landing at dusk, one in Lumenhold blue and one in Thornwick green, exchanging small wrapped parcels.
scene [ab4aec] = 黄昏时的驳船码头，两个学生，一个穿流明堡蓝，一个穿荆木绿，互相交换着小小的包裹。
# en: Give them yours
opt.left.label [e830e2] = 把你的那份给 TA
# en: You hand over the box you've kept under your bed for four years: every letter they sent, every insult, every postscript. They read the first one on the barge steps and laugh, and the barge leaves with them still laughing.
opt.left.say.1 [9b6365] = 你递过去那个在床底下放了四年的盒子：TA 寄来的每一封信，每一句损人话，每一则附言。TA 在驳船台阶上读了第一封就笑了起来，驳船载着还在笑的 TA 离开了。
# en: "Write to me. Same as ever."
opt.right.label [4bc311] = “给我写信。和以前一样。”
# en: "Every week," they promise. "Insufferably." The barge pulls away. They're still waving when it rounds the bend, and so are you.
opt.right.say.1 [056d39] = “每周一封，”TA 保证，“保证让人受不了。”驳船驶离。直到它转过河湾，TA 还在挥手，你也是。

@event intern_thornwick_tamsin
# en: A Familiar Hand
title [3d7a98] = 熟悉的笔迹
# en: On your first morning at the Thornwick lab, the student at the next bench looks up from a glowing illusion and grins. It's Tamsin. "They said a Lumenhold intern was coming," they say. "I told them it had better be you, or I'd sabotage everything."
text [2ccb5a] = 你在荆木实验室的第一个早上，隔壁工作台的学生从一个发光的幻象上抬起头，咧嘴一笑。是塔姆辛。“他们说要来个流明堡的实习生，”TA 说。“我告诉他们最好是你，不然我就把一切都搞砸。”
# en: A laboratory at a rival academy, a student in Thornwick green looking up from a glowing illusion on a bench, mid-grin, at a visitor in the doorway.
scene [1fa6b7] = 对手学院的一间实验室里，一个穿荆木绿的学生从工作台上发光的幻象抬起头，正咧着嘴笑向门口的访客。
# en: Work beside them all summer
opt.left.label [6a1618] = 整个夏天都在 TA 旁边干活
# en: A summer at the next bench. They show you every trick in Thornwick's book, and you show them three Lumenhold ones they swear aren't legal. Your supervisor calls you "the inseparables", not kindly.
opt.left.say.1 [1b9294] = 一个夏天都在隔壁工作台。TA 把荆木的每个诀窍都教给了你，你教了 TA 三个流明堡的，TA 发誓那些不合法。你的导师管你们叫“连体婴”，并不是夸奖。
# en: Keep it professional
opt.right.label [a540e8] = 保持公事公办
# en: You work at your own bench and keep your mind on the work. The lab notices; Tamsin notices more. "Fine," they say at the end. "You were right. But I missed you, at the next bench."
opt.right.say.1 [134fe0] = 你在自己的工作台干活，心思全放在工作上。实验室注意到了；塔姆辛注意到的更多。“好吧，”最后 TA 说。“你是对的。但我想念隔壁工作台上的你。”

@event lyra_on_thornwick
# en: Lyra on Thornwick
title [06748b] = 莱拉谈荆木
# en: Lyra has the Ledger folded to the contest results. "Thornwick," she says, as if it were a mild disease. {met(tamsin): "And you write letters to one of them. Every week. I've seen the green seals."|"I hope you enjoyed humiliating them. Or being humiliated. I was too angry to watch closely."}
text [4b0bc5] = 莱拉把《流明纪事报》折到比赛结果那一页。“荆木，”她说，像在说一种轻微的疾病。{met(tamsin): “而你每周都给他们中的一个写信。我看见那些绿色封蜡了。”|“希望你羞辱他们羞辱得愉快。或者被羞辱得愉快。我气得没法仔细看。”}
# en: A proud red-haired student sitting on a bench by the duelling hall, a newspaper folded to the contest results across her knee.
scene [e50666] = 一个骄傲的红发学生坐在决斗厅旁的长椅上，膝上横着一份折到比赛结果的报纸。
# en: Defend Thornwick
opt.left.label [3f76fa] = 为荆木说话
# en: You tell her Thornwick's people are people. She listens with enormous scepticism. A month later she asks, very casually, whether your Thornwick friend would ever want a practice duel. "For research," she says.
opt.left.say.1 [1cffd0] = 你告诉她，荆木的人也是人。她带着极大的怀疑听着。一个月后，她非常随意地问你，你那位荆木的朋友愿不愿意来一场练习决斗。“为了研究，”她说。
# en: Agree they're insufferable
opt.right.label [8f826f] = 同意他们让人受不了
# en: "Insufferable," you agree. She looks almost happy. "Exactly," she says. "Thank you." You don't tell Tamsin, who would agree with her.
opt.right.say.1 [686e93] = “让人受不了，”你附和道。她看起来几乎是高兴的。“没错，”她说。“谢谢你。”你没告诉塔姆辛，TA 会同意她的。
